logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store

# Every local env file, not only the two that happened to exist when this was
# written — `.env.production` and friends carry the same project keys and were
# not covered. `.env.example` is the tracked template and is the one exception.
.env*
!.env.example

# Firebase service account keys and client config — never commit
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# Android build output and local signing config. The keystore and its
# passwords never enter version control — see Plan 1 Task 5.
android/app/build/
android/build/
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
android/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# Build artifacts, wherever they are made. `android/.gitignore` already carries
# `*.apk`, but that rule only reaches inside `android/` — a release APK copied
# to the repo root to be side-loaded onto the phone went in with an unrelated
# fix and stayed, nine versions stale, in a public repo. Keep the copy on disk,
# not in the history: it is 35 MB every time, and a stale one is worse than
# none, because somebody downloads it and judges the wrong app.
*.apk
*.aab

# iOS build output lives in ios/.gitignore, which `cap add ios` wrote and
# which already covers Pods/, DerivedData and the copied web assets.

CLAUDE.md
docs/*
!docs/BUILDING.md
!docs/APPEARANCE.md

# Supabase CLI scratch. `linked-project.json` records the project ref and the
# organization id — nothing that grants access, but nothing the repo needs either.
supabase/.temp/

# Personal build notes: absolute SDK paths and an AVD name from one machine.
commands.md
